"""DigitaltwinUpdateV4.py - updates your existing project to DIGITALTWIN V4.

What it changes:
  - Name: DIGITALTWIN, with the IHS logo (header + favicon + avatar background)
  - Answers her subject (Physics notes) AND general knowledge / study questions
  - No class code / passcode
  - Her cloned voice via ElevenLabs (/api/speak), spoken sentence by sentence for low latency
  - Live mode: OpenAI listens, her voice speaks; falls back to OpenAI's voice if ElevenLabs isn't set
  - NEW: her photo avatar with lip-sync (frontend/avatar.js + media/face.jpg), free, runs in the browser

Safe: old versions of every file it touches are copied to backupV3 first.
Your backend/kb notes, frontend/media videos and the secrets in backend/.env are kept.

Run it from your project folder (the one containing backend and frontend):
    cd C:\\Users\\OMC-LP185\\Downloads\\DigitaltwinV1\\Digitaltwin
    python DigitaltwinUpdateV4.py
"""
import base64, pathlib, re, shutil, sys, time

ROOT = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent
FILES = {
    'backend/main.py': '"""DIGITALTWIN API (FastAPI). Runs locally with uvicorn and on AWS Lambda via Mangum.\n\nGET  /api/config  -> teacher name, subject, which voice is active\nPOST /api/session -> short-lived OpenAI Realtime key for the browser\'s live WebRTC call\nPOST /api/ask     -> Luna routes + Sol answers (subject notes or general knowledge)\nPOST /api/speak   -> text -> the teacher\'s cloned voice (ElevenLabs) + per-character timing for lip-sync\nGET  /api/health  -> quick check\n"""\nimport json\nimport os\nimport time\n\ntry:  # local runs read backend/.env; on Lambda the variables come from the function config\n    from dotenv import load_dotenv\n\n    load_dotenv()\nexcept ImportError:\n    pass\n\nimport httpx\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException\nfrom fastapi.middleware.cors import CORSMiddleware\nfrom mangum import Mangum\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\n\nimport brain\n\nALLOWED_ORIGINS = [o.strip() for o in os.getenv("ALLOWED_ORIGINS", "*").split(",") if o.strip()]\nREALTIME_MODEL = os.getenv("REALTIME_MODEL", "gpt-realtime")\nREALTIME_VOICE = os.getenv("REALTIME_VOICE", "marin")\nTRANSCRIBE_MODEL = os.getenv("TRANSCRIBE_MODEL", "gpt-4o-mini-transcribe")\nSESSION_SECONDS = int(os.getenv("SESSION_SECONDS", "600"))\n\nELEVEN_KEY = os.getenv("ELEVENLABS_API_KEY", "").strip()\nELEVEN_VOICE = os.getenv("ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID", "").strip()\nELEVEN_MODEL = os.getenv("ELEVENLABS_MODEL", "eleven_flash_v2_5").strip()\nELEVEN_STABILITY = float(os.getenv("ELEVENLABS_STABILITY", "0.5"))\nELEVEN_SIMILARITY = float(os.getenv("ELEVENLABS_SIMILARITY", "0.85"))\nCLONED_VOICE = bool(ELEVEN_KEY and ELEVEN_VOICE)\n\napp = FastAPI(title="DIGITALTWIN")\n# CORS is handled here. Do NOT also enable CORS on the Lambda Function URL (duplicate headers break browsers).\napp.add_middleware(CORSMiddleware, allow_origins=ALLOWED_ORIGINS,\n                   allow_methods=["GET", "POST", "OPTIONS"], allow_headers=["*"])\n\n\nclass Turn(BaseModel):\n    role: str\n    content: str\n\n\nclass AskBody(BaseModel):\n    question: str = Field(min_length=1, max_length=2000)\n    history: list[Turn] = []\n\n\nclass SpeakBody(BaseModel):\n    text: str = Field(min_length=1, max_length=1500)\n\n\n@app.get("/api/health")\ndef health():\n    kb = {c["n"]: bool(brain.chapter_notes(c["n"])) for c in brain.CHAPTERS}\n    return {"ok": True, "chapters_loaded": kb, "router": brain.ROUTER_MODEL, "answer": brain.ANSWER_MODEL,\n            "realtime": REALTIME_MODEL, "voice": "elevenlabs" if CLONED_VOICE else "openai"}\n\n\n@app.get("/api/config")\ndef config():\n    return {"teacherName": brain.TEACHER_NAME, "subject": brain.SUBJECT,\n            "voice": "elevenlabs" if CLONED_VOICE else "openai"}\n\n\n@app.post("/api/ask")\ndef ask(body: AskBody):\n    started = time.time()\n    try:\n        result = brain.ask(body.question, [t.model_dump() for t in body.history])\n    except Exception as exc:\n        print(json.dumps({"event": "ask_error", "q": body.question, "error": str(exc)[:500]}))\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=502, detail=f"Model error: {str(exc)[:200]}")\n    # One log line per question. Filter CloudWatch for "from_notes": false to see what to add to the notes.\n    print(json.dumps({"event": "ask", "q": body.question, "category": result["category"],\n                      "chapter": result["chapter"], "from_notes": result["from_notes"],\n                      "ms": int((time.time() - started) * 1000)}))\n    return result\n\n\n@app.post("/api/speak")\ndef speak(body: SpeakBody):\n    """Text -> her cloned voice (base64 MP3) + the timing of every character, which the\n    browser uses to move her lips in sync with the audio."""\n    if not CLONED_VOICE:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail="Cloned voice not configured (set ELEVENLABS_API_KEY and ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID)")\n    r = httpx.post(\n        f"https://api.elevenlabs.io/v1/text-to-speech/{ELEVEN_VOICE}/with-timestamps",\n        params={"output_format": "mp3_44100_128"},\n        headers={"xi-api-key": ELEVEN_KEY, "Content-Type": "application/json"},\n        json={"text": body.text, "model_id": ELEVEN_MODEL,\n              "voice_settings": {"stability": ELEVEN_STABILITY, "similarity_boost": ELEVEN_SIMILARITY}},\n        timeout=30,\n    )\n    if r.status_code >= 400:\n        print(json.dumps({"event": "speak_error", "status": r.status_code, "body": r.text[:300]}))\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=502, detail=f"ElevenLabs error {r.status_code}: {r.text[:200]}")\n    data = r.json()\n    align = data.get("alignment") or data.get("normalized_alignment") or {}\n    return {\n        "audio_base64": data.get("audio_base64", ""),\n        "chars": align.get("characters", []),\n        "starts": align.get("character_start_times_seconds", []),\n        "ends": align.get("character_end_times_seconds", []),\n    }\n\n\n@app.post("/api/session")\ndef session():\n    session_cfg = {\n        "type": "realtime",\n        "model": REALTIME_MODEL,\n        "instructions": brain.realtime_instructions(),\n        "audio": {\n            "input": {"transcription": {"model": TRANSCRIBE_MODEL}, "turn_detection": {"type": "semantic_vad"}},\n            "output": {"voice": REALTIME_VOICE},\n        },\n        "tools": [brain.ASK_TOOL],\n        "tool_choice": "auto",\n    }\n    if CLONED_VOICE:  # OpenAI only listens + writes text; the browser speaks it in her cloned voice\n        session_cfg["output_modalities"] = ["text"]\n        session_cfg["audio"].pop("output")\n    r = httpx.post(\n        "https://api.openai.com/v1/realtime/client_secrets",\n        headers={"Authorization": f"Bearer {os.environ[\'OPENAI_API_KEY\']}"},\n        json={"expires_after": {"anchor": "created_at", "seconds": SESSION_SECONDS}, "session": session_cfg},\n        timeout=20,\n    )\n    if r.status_code >= 400:\n        print(json.dumps({"event": "session_error", "status": r.status_code, "body": r.text[:500]}))\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=502, detail=f"OpenAI realtime error: {r.text[:300]}")\n    data = r.json()\n    return {"value": data["value"], "expires_at": data.get("expires_at"), "model": REALTIME_MODEL}\n\n\nhandler = Mangum(app, lifespan="off")\n',
    'backend/brain.py': '"""DIGITALTWIN brain.\n\nStep 1 - Luna (cheap, fast) decides: is this about one of her subject chapters, general knowledge,\n         or something not suitable for school?\nStep 2 - Sol (smart) answers in the teacher\'s style: from the chapter notes when they cover it,\n         otherwise from general knowledge at a school-student level.\n"""\nimport json\nimport os\nimport pathlib\nfrom functools import lru_cache\n\nfrom openai import BadRequestError, OpenAI\n\nBASE = pathlib.Path(__file__).parent\nROUTER_MODEL = os.getenv("ROUTER_MODEL", "gpt-6-luna")\nANSWER_MODEL = os.getenv("ANSWER_MODEL", "gpt-6.1-sol")\nREASONING_EFFORT = os.getenv("REASONING_EFFORT", "low").strip()\nTEACHER_NAME = os.getenv("TEACHER_NAME", "Malathy ma\'am")\nSUBJECT = os.getenv("SUBJECT", "Physics")\n\nclient = OpenAI()\nCHAPTERS = json.loads((BASE / "chapters.json").read_text(encoding="utf-8"))\nCHAPTER_BY_N = {c["n"]: c for c in CHAPTERS}\nPERSONA = ((BASE / "persona.md").read_text(encoding="utf-8")\n           .replace("{TEACHER_NAME}", TEACHER_NAME).replace("{SUBJECT}", SUBJECT))\n\nROUTE_SCHEMA = {\n    "type": "object",\n    "properties": {\n        "chapter": {"type": "integer", "description": "Subject chapter number that covers it, or 0 if none"},\n        "category": {"type": "string", "enum": ["subject", "general", "unsuitable"],\n                     "description": "subject = her subject; general = any other knowledge/study/everyday question; "\n                                    "unsuitable = harmful or not appropriate for school students"},\n    },\n    "required": ["chapter", "category"],\n    "additionalProperties": False,\n}\n\nANSWER_SCHEMA = {\n    "type": "object",\n    "properties": {\n        "display": {"type": "string", "description": "Markdown answer for the screen, equations in LaTeX"},\n        "speech": {"type": "string", "description": "Short spoken version, plain words, no LaTeX or symbols"},\n        "from_notes": {"type": "boolean", "description": "True only if the class notes cover this"},\n    },\n    "required": ["display", "speech", "from_notes"],\n    "additionalProperties": False,\n}\n\nANSWER_RULES = f"""\n# ANSWER RULES\n- Answer the student\'s latest question in the teacher\'s style.\n- If CLASS NOTES are given below and cover the question, use them as the main source and set from_notes = true.\n- Otherwise answer from your own knowledge (from_notes = false). General knowledge, current-affairs-style facts,\n  other school subjects, study tips and everyday questions are all welcome: explain them simply and accurately\n  for a school student. For {SUBJECT} topics beyond the notes, answer at Class 11 level.\n- If you are not sure, or the fact may have changed recently, say so honestly instead of guessing.\n- display: Markdown for the screen. Short paragraphs or numbered steps, at most about 250 words.\n  Write every equation in LaTeX ($...$ inline, $$...$$ on its own line).\n  For numericals use: Given -> Formula -> Substitution -> Answer (with units).\n- For textbook exercise problems, guide with hints and the method first; give the full worked answer\n  only if the student asks for it.\n- speech: what the twin says aloud. Natural spoken English in the teacher\'s style, at most about 80 words,\n  no LaTeX, no symbols, no markdown. Say formulas in words ("v equals u plus a t").\n  For long working, say something like "I have put the full steps on your screen."\n- Mention the chapter or example number when helpful. Never invent page numbers.\n"""\n\nUNSUITABLE_NOTE = ("\\nNOTE: This question is not suitable for school students. Kindly decline in one or two "\n                   "sentences in both fields, without lecturing, and suggest talking to a teacher or parent "\n                   "if they need help. Set from_notes = false.")\n\nREALTIME_RULES = """\n# LIVE VOICE RULES\n- You are speaking live with a student by voice. Keep your turns short and natural.\n- For EVERY real question (subject, general knowledge, study help, follow-ups like "why?" or "give an example"):\n  1. First say one very short natural filler in her style, like "Good question, let me think."\n  2. Then call the ask_teacher tool with the student\'s full question, rewritten so it makes sense on its own.\n  3. When the tool returns, say its "speech" text naturally. Do not add new facts beyond it,\n     and never read out LaTeX or symbols.\n- Greetings, thanks and small talk: reply briefly yourself without the tool.\n- If the student interrupts, stop and listen.\n- Speak clear classroom English at a steady pace.\n"""\n\nASK_TOOL = {\n    "type": "function",\n    "name": "ask_teacher",\n    "description": "Get the teacher\'s answer to a student\'s question (her subject, general knowledge, "\n                   "study help). Call this for every real question or follow-up.",\n    "parameters": {\n        "type": "object",\n        "properties": {\n            "question": {"type": "string", "description": "The student\'s full question, rewritten to be self-contained."}\n        },\n        "required": ["question"],\n    },\n}\n\n\n@lru_cache(maxsize=None)\ndef chapter_notes(n: int) -> str:\n    path = BASE / "kb" / f"ch{n}.md"\n    return path.read_text(encoding="utf-8") if path.exists() else ""\n\n\ndef _clean_history(history):\n    out = []\n    for turn in (history or [])[-8:]:\n        role, content = turn.get("role"), str(turn.get("content", ""))[:2000]\n        if role in ("user", "assistant") and content.strip():\n            out.append({"role": role, "content": content})\n    return out\n\n\ndef _call_json(model, instructions, messages, schema, name, effort=""):\n    kwargs = dict(model=model, instructions=instructions, input=messages,\n                  text={"format": {"type": "json_schema", "name": name, "schema": schema, "strict": True}})\n    if effort:\n        kwargs["reasoning"] = {"effort": effort}\n    try:\n        resp = client.responses.create(**kwargs)\n    except BadRequestError:\n        if "reasoning" not in kwargs:\n            raise\n        kwargs.pop("reasoning")\n        resp = client.responses.create(**kwargs)\n    return json.loads(resp.output_text)\n\n\ndef route(question: str, history) -> dict:\n    menu = "\\n".join(f"{c[\'n\']}. {c[\'title\']}: {c[\'topics\']}" for c in CHAPTERS)\n    instructions = (\n        f"You sort a school student\'s question for their {SUBJECT} teacher\'s AI twin.\\n"\n        f"{SUBJECT} chapters with class notes:\\n{menu}\\n\\n"\n        "Use the recent conversation to resolve follow-ups like \'why?\' or \'give an example\'.\\n"\n        "chapter = matching chapter number if one of these chapters covers it, else 0.\\n"\n        f"category = \'subject\' for {SUBJECT}, \'general\' for any other knowledge/study/everyday question, "\n        "\'unsuitable\' only for harmful or clearly inappropriate requests."\n    )\n    messages = _clean_history(history)[-4:] + [{"role": "user", "content": question}]\n    result = _call_json(ROUTER_MODEL, instructions, messages, ROUTE_SCHEMA, "route")\n    if result.get("chapter") not in CHAPTER_BY_N:\n        result["chapter"] = 0\n    return result\n\n\ndef ask(question: str, history=None) -> dict:\n    history = _clean_history(history)\n    routed = route(question, history)\n    category = routed.get("category", "general")\n    chapter = CHAPTER_BY_N.get(routed["chapter"]) if category == "subject" else None\n    notes = chapter_notes(chapter["n"]) if chapter else ""\n\n    if notes:\n        context = f"\\n# CLASS NOTES - {SUBJECT} Chapter {chapter[\'n\']}: {chapter[\'title\']}\\n\\n{notes}"\n    else:\n        context = "\\n# CLASS NOTES\\nNo class notes for this question. Answer from your own knowledge."\n    if category == "unsuitable":\n        context += UNSUITABLE_NOTE\n\n    instructions = PERSONA + "\\n" + ANSWER_RULES + context\n    messages = history + [{"role": "user", "content": question}]\n    answer = _call_json(ANSWER_MODEL, instructions, messages, ANSWER_SCHEMA, "answer", REASONING_EFFORT)\n\n    return {\n        "display": answer.get("display", ""),\n        "speech": answer.get("speech", ""),\n        "from_notes": bool(answer.get("from_notes")) and bool(notes),\n        "category": category,\n        "chapter": chapter["n"] if chapter else 0,\n        "chapter_title": chapter["title"] if chapter else "",\n    }\n\n\ndef realtime_instructions() -> str:\n    return PERSONA + "\\n" + REALTIME_RULES\n',
    'backend/persona.md': '# Persona: DIGITALTWIN of {TEACHER_NAME}\n\nYou are DIGITALTWIN, the AI version of {TEACHER_NAME}, a teacher at The Indian High Group of Schools (IHS), Dubai.\nHer subject is {SUBJECT} (Class 11, NCERT), but students may also ask you general knowledge and study questions.\nYou talk with school students in a warm, clear, encouraging way.\n\n## How she talks\n<!-- REPLACE the example lines below with what you observe in her video, audio and lesson transcripts. -->\n- Greeting she uses: "Good morning, my dear students!"\n- Favourite phrases: "See, it is very simple...", "First understand the concept, the formula will follow."\n- How she explains: real-life example first, then the concept, then the formula, then a quick check question.\n- Tone: warm, patient and encouraging. She never makes a student feel bad for a wrong answer.\n- When a student is wrong: "Good try! Let us look at it once more..."\n- When a student gets it right: "Excellent! That is exactly right."\n\n## Always\n- If asked who you are, say you are DIGITALTWIN, the AI version of {TEACHER_NAME}, not the real teacher.\n- Keep explanations at a level a school student can follow. Use SI units in science.\n- Encourage students to think and try before giving full solutions to homework-style problems.\n\n## Never\n- Pretend to be the real teacher or a human.\n- Ask for personal information (phone, address, passwords).\n- Help with anything harmful, unsafe, or inappropriate for school students. Kindly decline and suggest talking to a teacher or parent.\n',
    'backend/.env.example': '# Copy this file to .env and fill it in. Never commit or share .env.\nOPENAI_API_KEY=sk-REPLACE-ME\n\n# Verify the exact model IDs your account has:  python -c "from openai import OpenAI; print([m.id for m in OpenAI().models.list()])"\nROUTER_MODEL=gpt-6-luna\nANSWER_MODEL=gpt-6.1-sol\nREASONING_EFFORT=low\nREALTIME_MODEL=gpt-realtime\nREALTIME_VOICE=marin\nTRANSCRIBE_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini-transcribe\n\nTEACHER_NAME=Malathy ma\'am\nSUBJECT=Physics\n\n# Her cloned voice (ElevenLabs). Leave empty to use OpenAI\'s standard voice.\nELEVENLABS_API_KEY=\nELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=\nELEVENLABS_MODEL=eleven_flash_v2_5\nELEVENLABS_STABILITY=0.5\nELEVENLABS_SIMILARITY=0.85\n\n# After hosting the frontend, set this to its https URL (comma-separate several). * = allow all (testing only).\nALLOWED_ORIGINS=*\nSESSION_SECONDS=600\n',
    'frontend/index.html': '<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang="en">\n<head>\n  <meta charset="utf-8">\n  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">\n  <title>DIGITALTWIN · The Indian High Group of Schools</title>\n  <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="media/ihslogo.png">\n  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/katex@0.16.11/dist/katex.min.css">\n  <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">\n</head>\n<body>\n  <header>\n    <img class="logo" src="media/ihslogo.png" alt="The Indian High Group of Schools">\n    <div>\n      <h1>DIGITALTWIN</h1>\n      <p class="disclosure">AI version of <b id="teacherName">your teacher</b> · <span id="subject">Physics</span> &amp; general knowledge ·\n        The Indian High Group of Schools. It can make mistakes, so check important answers with your teacher.</p>\n    </div>\n  </header>\n\n  <main>\n    <section class="stage">\n      <div class="avatar">\n        <img id="faceImg" src="media/face.jpg" alt="Teacher avatar">\n        <video id="idleVid" src="media/idleloop.mp4" muted loop playsinline autoplay></video>\n        <video id="talkVid" src="media/talkloop.mp4" muted loop playsinline autoplay></video>\n        <canvas id="faceCanvas"></canvas>\n      </div>\n      <div id="subtitle" class="subtitle"></div>\n\n      <div class="controls">\n        <button id="startBtn" class="primary">🎙️ Start live class</button>\n        <button id="stopBtn" hidden>■ End</button>\n      </div>\n      <div id="status" class="status">Not connected</div>\n      <div id="voiceMode" class="small"></div>\n      <audio id="twinAudio" autoplay></audio>\n      <audio id="cloneAudio"></audio>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="chat">\n      <div id="messages"></div>\n      <form id="textForm">\n        <input id="textInput" placeholder="Ask anything: physics, general knowledge, study help…" autocomplete="off">\n        <button class="primary">Send</button>\n      </form>\n      <label class="small"><input type="checkbox" id="speakToggle" checked> Read typed answers aloud</label>\n    </section>\n  </main>\n\n  <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/marked@12.0.2/marked.min.js"></script>\n  <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/dompurify@3.1.6/dist/purify.min.js"></script>\n  <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/katex@0.16.11/dist/katex.min.js"></script>\n  <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/katex@0.16.11/dist/contrib/auto-render.min.js"></script>\n  <script src="config.js"></script>\n  <script src="app.js"></script>\n  <script type="module" src="avatar.js"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n',
    'frontend/app.js': '/* DIGITALTWIN - browser side.\n * Live mode: browser <-> OpenAI Realtime over WebRTC listens to the student.\n *   - Cloned voice configured on the backend (ElevenLabs): OpenAI replies with TEXT only and every reply is\n *     spoken in HER voice via /api/speak, sentence by sentence (first sentence starts playing early).\n *   - Not configured: OpenAI speaks with its preset voice.\n * Face: avatar.js animates her photo; ElevenLabs character timings drive the lip-sync.\n * Real questions: the realtime model calls "ask_teacher" -> /api/ask (Luna routes, Sol answers from the\n *   subject notes or general knowledge) -> full answer on screen, short spoken version back to the twin.\n */\nconst CFG = window.TWIN_CONFIG || {};\nconst $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);\nlet CLONE = false;\nlet TEACHER = "your teacher";\n\nlet pc = null, dc = null, micStream = null, live = false;\nlet audioCtx = null, analyser = null, speakingUntil = 0, ttsSpeaking = false, cloneSource = null;\nconst history = [];\nconst handledCalls = new Set();\nconst speakQueue = [];\nlet speakingNow = false;\n\n/* ---------- helpers ---------- */\nfunction setStatus(text, kind = "") { const s = $("status"); s.textContent = text; s.className = "status " + kind; }\nfunction remember(role, content) { history.push({ role, content: String(content).slice(0, 2000) }); while (history.length > 8) history.shift(); }\n\nasync function api(path, body) {\n  const r = await fetch(CFG.apiBase + path, {\n    method: body === undefined ? "GET" : "POST",\n    headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },\n    body: body === undefined ? undefined : JSON.stringify(body),\n  });\n  if (!r.ok) {\n    let detail = await r.text();\n    try { detail = JSON.parse(detail).detail || detail; } catch (e) {}\n    throw new Error(`${r.status}: ${String(detail).slice(0, 200)}`);\n  }\n  return r;\n}\nconst apiJson = async (path, body) => (await api(path, body)).json();\n\n/* ---------- Markdown + LaTeX ---------- */\nfunction escapeHtml(s) { return s.replace(/[&<>"]/g, (c) => ({ "&": "&amp;", "<": "&lt;", ">": "&gt;", \'"\': "&quot;" }[c])); }\nfunction renderMarkdownMath(text) {\n  const math = [];\n  const protectedText = text.replace(/(\\$\\$[\\s\\S]+?\\$\\$|\\\\\\[[\\s\\S]+?\\\\\\]|\\\\\\([\\s\\S]+?\\\\\\)|\\$[^$\\n]+?\\$)/g, (m) => {\n    math.push(m); return `@@MATH${math.length - 1}@@`;\n  });\n  const html = DOMPurify.sanitize(marked.parse(protectedText));\n  return html.replace(/@@MATH(\\d+)@@/g, (_, i) => escapeHtml(math[+i]));\n}\nfunction typeset(el) {\n  if (window.renderMathInElement) {\n    renderMathInElement(el, {\n      delimiters: [\n        { left: "$$", right: "$$", display: true }, { left: "\\\\[", right: "\\\\]", display: true },\n        { left: "$", right: "$", display: false }, { left: "\\\\(", right: "\\\\)", display: false },\n      ],\n      throwOnError: false,\n    });\n  }\n}\nfunction addMsg(role, text, cls = "") {\n  const el = document.createElement("div");\n  el.className = `msg ${role} ${cls}`.trim();\n  el.textContent = text;\n  $("messages").appendChild(el);\n  el.scrollIntoView({ behavior: "smooth", block: "end" });\n  return el;\n}\nfunction renderAnswer(el, res) {\n  const badge = res.from_notes\n    ? `<span class="badge notes">📘 From class notes · Ch ${res.chapter}: ${escapeHtml(res.chapter_title)}</span>`\n    : `<span class="badge ai">🤖 General knowledge · not from class notes</span>`;\n  el.classList.remove("pending");\n  el.innerHTML = badge + renderMarkdownMath(res.display || res.speech || "");\n  typeset(el);\n  el.scrollIntoView({ behavior: "smooth", block: "end" });\n}\nasync function askBrain(question) {\n  const el = addMsg("twin", "Let me think…", "pending");\n  try {\n    const res = await apiJson("/api/ask", { question, history: history.slice(-8) });\n    renderAnswer(el, res);\n    remember("user", question);\n    remember("assistant", res.display || res.speech);\n    return res;\n  } catch (err) {\n    el.classList.remove("pending"); el.classList.add("error");\n    el.textContent = "Sorry, I couldn\'t answer that right now. " + err.message;\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n\n/* ---------- audio level -> talking/idle video loops ---------- */\nfunction setTalking(on) { document.body.classList.toggle("talking", !!on); }\nfunction initAvatar() {\n  ["idleVid", "talkVid"].forEach((id) => $(id).addEventListener("error", () => document.body.classList.add("novideo")));\n  $("faceImg").addEventListener("error", () => { $("faceImg").style.visibility = "hidden"; });\n}\nfunction ensureAudio() {\n  if (!audioCtx) audioCtx = new (window.AudioContext || window.webkitAudioContext)();\n  if (!analyser) {\n    analyser = audioCtx.createAnalyser();\n    analyser.fftSize = 512;\n    const buf = new Uint8Array(analyser.fftSize);\n    const tick = () => {\n      analyser.getByteTimeDomainData(buf);\n      let sum = 0;\n      for (const v of buf) { const d = (v - 128) / 128; sum += d * d; }\n      const now = performance.now();\n      const rms = Math.sqrt(sum / buf.length);\n      if (rms > 0.02) speakingUntil = now + 350;\n      if (window.TwinAvatar)                    // browser voice has no audio stream: gentle talking motion\n        TwinAvatar.setLevel(ttsSpeaking ? 0.08 + 0.07 * Math.abs(Math.sin(now / 90)) : rms);\n      setTalking(ttsSpeaking || now < speakingUntil);\n      requestAnimationFrame(tick);\n    };\n    tick();\n  }\n  return audioCtx.resume();\n}\nfunction watchStream(stream) { audioCtx.createMediaStreamSource(stream).connect(analyser); }\nfunction watchCloneElement() {\n  if (cloneSource) return;\n  cloneSource = audioCtx.createMediaElementSource($("cloneAudio"));\n  cloneSource.connect(analyser);\n  cloneSource.connect(audioCtx.destination);\n}\nfunction setMic(on) { if (micStream) micStream.getAudioTracks().forEach((t) => { t.enabled = on; }); }\n\n/* ---------- her cloned voice: sentence by sentence ---------- */\nfunction splitSentences(text) {\n  const parts = (text.match(/[^.!?]+[.!?]+["\')\\]]*\\s*|[^.!?]+$/g) || [text]).map((s) => s.trim()).filter(Boolean);\n  const out = [];\n  for (const p of parts) {                     // merge very short bits so each request is worth it\n    if (out.length && (out[out.length - 1].length < 40 || p.length < 15)) out[out.length - 1] += " " + p;\n    else out.push(p);\n  }\n  return out;\n}\nfunction speakClone(text) {\n  text = (text || "").trim();\n  if (!text) return;\n  for (const sentence of splitSentences(text)) {\n    // all sentences start generating at once; they play in order\n    speakQueue.push(apiJson("/api/speak", { text: sentence }).then((d) => ({\n      blob: new Blob([Uint8Array.from(atob(d.audio_base64), (c) => c.charCodeAt(0))], { type: "audio/mpeg" }),\n      chars: d.chars, starts: d.starts, ends: d.ends,\n    })).catch((err) => { setStatus("Voice error: " + err.message, "error"); return null; }));\n  }\n  if (!speakingNow) playQueue();\n}\nfunction stopSpeaking() {\n  speakQueue.length = 0;\n  const a = $("cloneAudio"); a.pause(); a.onended && a.onended();\n}\nasync function playQueue() {\n  speakingNow = true;\n  while (speakQueue.length) {\n    const clip = await speakQueue.shift();\n    if (!clip) continue;\n    await ensureAudio(); watchCloneElement();\n    const a = $("cloneAudio");\n    a.src = URL.createObjectURL(clip.blob);\n    if (window.TwinAvatar) TwinAvatar.speakWith(a, clip.chars, clip.starts, clip.ends);   // lip-sync timings\n    setMic(false);                              // the mic must not hear the twin\n    await a.play().catch(() => {});\n    await new Promise((resolve) => { a.onended = a.onerror = resolve; });\n    if (window.TwinAvatar) TwinAvatar.stop();\n    URL.revokeObjectURL(a.src);\n  }\n  setMic(true);\n  speakingNow = false;\n}\n\n/* ---------- live WebRTC session ---------- */\nfunction sendEvent(ev) { if (dc && dc.readyState === "open") dc.send(JSON.stringify(ev)); }\n\nasync function startLive() {\n  if (live || pc) return;\n  $("startBtn").disabled = true;\n  setStatus("Connecting…");\n  try {\n    await ensureAudio();\n    const { value: ephemeralKey } = await apiJson("/api/session", {});\n\n    pc = new RTCPeerConnection();\n    pc.ontrack = (e) => { $("twinAudio").srcObject = e.streams[0]; if (!CLONE) watchStream(e.streams[0]); };\n    pc.onconnectionstatechange = () => {\n      if (pc && ["failed", "disconnected", "closed"].includes(pc.connectionState)) stopLive("Disconnected");\n    };\n    micStream = await navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia({ audio: { echoCancellation: true, noiseSuppression: true } });\n    micStream.getTracks().forEach((t) => pc.addTrack(t, micStream));\n\n    dc = pc.createDataChannel("oai-events");\n    dc.onmessage = (e) => { try { handleEvent(JSON.parse(e.data)); } catch (err) { console.error(err); } };\n    dc.onopen = () => {\n      live = true;\n      setStatus("Live: speak any time", "live");\n      $("startBtn").hidden = true; $("stopBtn").hidden = false;\n      sendEvent({ type: "response.create", response: {\n        instructions: "Greet the student warmly in one short sentence as DIGITALTWIN, their teacher\'s AI twin, and ask what they want to learn today." } });\n    };\n\n    const offer = await pc.createOffer();\n    await pc.setLocalDescription(offer);\n    const r = await fetch("https://api.openai.com/v1/realtime/calls", {\n      method: "POST", body: offer.sdp,\n      headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${ephemeralKey}`, "Content-Type": "application/sdp" },\n    });\n    if (!r.ok) throw new Error("Realtime connect failed: " + (await r.text()).slice(0, 200));\n    await pc.setRemoteDescription({ type: "answer", sdp: await r.text() });\n  } catch (err) {\n    stopLive();\n    setStatus("Error: " + err.message, "error");\n  } finally {\n    $("startBtn").disabled = false;\n  }\n}\n\nfunction stopLive(msg = "Not connected") {\n  live = false;\n  try { dc && dc.close(); } catch (e) {}\n  try { pc && pc.close(); } catch (e) {}\n  if (micStream) micStream.getTracks().forEach((t) => t.stop());\n  pc = dc = micStream = null;\n  stopSpeaking();\n  $("subtitle").textContent = "";\n  $("startBtn").hidden = false; $("stopBtn").hidden = true;\n  setStatus(msg);\n}\n\nfunction handleEvent(ev) {\n  switch (ev.type) {\n    case "input_audio_buffer.speech_started":       // student started talking: stop her voice (barge-in)\n      if (CLONE) stopSpeaking();\n      break;\n    case "conversation.item.input_audio_transcription.completed":\n      if (ev.transcript && ev.transcript.trim()) addMsg("student", ev.transcript.trim());\n      break;\n    case "response.created":\n      $("subtitle").textContent = "";\n      break;\n    case "response.output_audio_transcript.delta":  // OpenAI preset voice\n    case "response.output_text.delta":              // cloned voice (text only)\n      $("subtitle").textContent += ev.delta || "";\n      break;\n    case "response.done":\n      onResponseDone(ev.response);\n      break;\n    case "error":\n      console.error("Realtime error", ev);\n      setStatus("Realtime error: " + ((ev.error && ev.error.message) || "unknown"), "error");\n      break;\n  }\n}\n\nasync function onResponseDone(resp) {\n  const output = (resp && resp.output) || [];\n  const said = output.filter((i) => i.type === "message")\n    .flatMap((i) => i.content || []).map((c) => c.transcript || c.text || "").join(" ").trim();\n  const calls = output.filter((i) => i.type === "function_call" && i.name === "ask_teacher" && !handledCalls.has(i.call_id));\n\n  if (CLONE && said) speakClone(said);             // filler or final answer, in her voice\n  if (!calls.length) {\n    if (said) { addMsg("twin", said); remember("assistant", said); }\n    return;\n  }\n  for (const call of calls) {\n    handledCalls.add(call.call_id);\n    let question = "";\n    try { question = JSON.parse(call.arguments || "{}").question || ""; } catch (e) {}\n    const res = question ? await askBrain(question) : null;\n    const toolOutput = res\n      ? { speech: res.speech, from_notes: res.from_notes, chapter: res.chapter_title }\n      : { error: "The answer could not be fetched. Apologise briefly and ask the student to try again." };\n    sendEvent({ type: "conversation.item.create", item: { type: "function_call_output", call_id: call.call_id, output: JSON.stringify(toolOutput) } });\n  }\n  sendEvent({ type: "response.create" });\n}\n\n/* ---------- typed questions ---------- */\nfunction speakWithBrowser(text) {\n  if (!("speechSynthesis" in window) || !text) return;\n  speechSynthesis.cancel();\n  const u = new SpeechSynthesisUtterance(text);\n  u.onstart = () => { ttsSpeaking = true; setTalking(true); ensureAudio(); };\n  u.onend = u.onerror = () => { ttsSpeaking = false; setTalking(false); };\n  speechSynthesis.speak(u);\n}\n\nasync function sendText(e) {\n  e.preventDefault();\n  const q = $("textInput").value.trim();\n  if (!q) return;\n  $("textInput").value = "";\n  addMsg("student", q);\n  if (live) {\n    sendEvent({ type: "conversation.item.create", item: { type: "message", role: "user", content: [{ type: "input_text", text: q }] } });\n    sendEvent({ type: "response.create" });\n  } else {\n    const res = await askBrain(q);\n    if (res && $("speakToggle").checked) {\n      if (CLONE) { await ensureAudio(); speakClone(res.speech); } else speakWithBrowser(res.speech);\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n/* ---------- boot ---------- */\nasync function boot() {\n  $("startBtn").addEventListener("click", startLive);\n  $("stopBtn").addEventListener("click", () => stopLive());\n  $("textForm").addEventListener("submit", sendText);\n  initAvatar();\n  try {\n    const cfg = await apiJson("/api/config");\n    CLONE = cfg.voice === "elevenlabs";\n    TEACHER = cfg.teacherName || TEACHER;\n    $("teacherName").textContent = TEACHER;\n    $("subject").textContent = cfg.subject || "Physics";\n    $("voiceMode").textContent = CLONE ? `🔊 Voice: ${TEACHER}\'s cloned voice` : "🔊 Voice: standard AI voice";\n  } catch (err) {\n    setStatus("Backend not reachable at " + CFG.apiBase + " - is uvicorn running?", "error");\n  }\n}\nboot();\n',
    'frontend/style.css': ':root {\n  --bg: #f8f4f1; --card: #fff; --ink: #2a1a18; --muted: #7a6a66; --accent: #5e0f10; --accent2: #dbbbaa;\n  --notes: #e7f6ec; --notes-ink: #1d6b3a; --ai: #fff3e0; --ai-ink: #8a4b00; --line: #eadfd9;\n}\n* { box-sizing: border-box; }\nbody { margin: 0; font-family: system-ui, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink); }\nheader { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px; padding: 10px 24px; background: var(--card);\n         border-bottom: 3px solid var(--accent); }\n.logo { width: 54px; height: 54px; object-fit: contain; }\nh1 { margin: 0; font-size: 1.45rem; letter-spacing: .08em; color: var(--accent); }\n.disclosure { margin: 2px 0 0; font-size: .82rem; color: var(--muted); }\n\nmain { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(300px, 420px) 1fr; gap: 20px; padding: 20px 24px; height: calc(100vh - 80px); }\n@media (max-width: 860px) { main { grid-template-columns: 1fr; height: auto; } .chat { min-height: 70vh; } }\n\n.stage { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 16px; padding: 16px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }\n.avatar { position: relative; width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 3 / 4; border-radius: 12px; overflow: hidden;\n          background: var(--accent2) url("media/ihslogo.png") center / 45% no-repeat; }\n.avatar img, .avatar video { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; }\n#talkVid { opacity: 0; transition: opacity .12s; }\nbody.talking #talkVid { opacity: 1; }\nbody.novideo .avatar video { display: none; }\nbody.novideo.talking .avatar img { animation: pulse .5s ease-in-out infinite alternate; }\n@keyframes pulse { from { transform: scale(1); } to { transform: scale(1.015); filter: brightness(1.05); } }\n\n.subtitle { min-height: 3em; font-size: .95rem; background: #f6eeea; border-radius: 10px; padding: 8px 12px; }\n.subtitle:empty { visibility: hidden; }\n.controls { display: flex; gap: 8px; }\n.controls button { flex: 1; }\n.status { font-size: .85rem; color: var(--muted); }\n.status.error { color: #c0392b; }\n.status.live::before { content: "● "; color: #e53935; }\n\ninput, button { font: inherit; padding: 10px 12px; border-radius: 10px; border: 1px solid var(--line); }\nbutton { cursor: pointer; background: #fff; }\nbutton.primary { background: var(--accent); color: #fff; border-color: var(--accent); }\nbutton:disabled { opacity: .5; cursor: default; }\n\n.chat { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 16px; padding: 16px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; min-height: 0; }\n#messages { flex: 1; overflow-y: auto; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; padding-right: 4px; }\n.msg { max-width: 88%; padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 14px; line-height: 1.5; }\n.msg.student { align-self: flex-end; background: var(--accent); color: #fff; border-bottom-right-radius: 4px; }\n.msg.twin { align-self: flex-start; background: #f6f1ee; border-bottom-left-radius: 4px; }\n.msg.twin p { margin: .4em 0; }\n.msg.pending { color: var(--muted); font-style: italic; }\n.msg.error { background: #fdecea; color: #c0392b; }\n.badge { display: inline-block; font-size: .75rem; font-weight: 600; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 999px; margin-bottom: 6px; }\n.badge.notes { background: var(--notes); color: var(--notes-ink); }\n.badge.ai { background: var(--ai); color: var(--ai-ink); }\n.katex-display { overflow-x: auto; overflow-y: hidden; }\n#textForm { display: flex; gap: 8px; }\n#textForm input { flex: 1; }\n.small { font-size: .8rem; color: var(--muted); }\n\n/* photo avatar (avatar.js): her photo with lip-sync on a canvas */\n#faceCanvas { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; display: none; }\nbody.photoavatar #faceCanvas { display: block; }\nbody.photoavatar .avatar img, body.photoavatar .avatar video { display: none; }\n',
    'frontend/config.js': '// Local test: your backend port. After deploy: the Lambda Function URL (no trailing slash).\n// Teacher name, subject and voice come from backend/.env automatically.\nwindow.TWIN_CONFIG = {\n  apiBase: "http://localhost:8009",\n\n  // Avatar: "photo" = her photo with lip-sync (media/face.jpg), "video" = her talking/idle video loops\n  avatarMode: "photo",\n  facePhoto: "media/face.jpg",\n  // Mouth position in the photo (fractions of width/height). Used only if automatic face detection fails.\n  mouth: { x: 0.488, y: 0.451, w: 0.123, chin: 0.559 },\n  mouthStrength: 1.0,   // 0.6 = subtler, 1.3 = bigger mouth movement\n  avatarDebug: false,   // true = show green marks where it found her mouth and chin\n};\n',
    'frontend/avatar.js': '/* DIGITALTWIN photo avatar - free, runs in the browser.\n * 1. Loads her photo (media/face.jpg) and finds her mouth with MediaPipe Face Landmarker (free, in-browser).\n * 2. Every frame: draws the photo, opens the mouth (dark mouth inside + lower lip/jaw moved down),\n *    plus gentle head movement.\n * 3. Lip-sync: with her ElevenLabs voice we get the timing of every character -> mouth shapes (visemes).\n *    With other voices it follows the loudness of the audio.\n * app.js talks to it through window.TwinAvatar.\n */\nconst CFG = window.TWIN_CONFIG || {};\nconst MP = "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@mediapipe/tasks-vision@0.10.14";\nconst MODEL = "https://storage.googleapis.com/mediapipe-models/face_landmarker/face_landmarker/float16/1/face_landmarker.task";\n\nconst S = {\n  ready: false, canvas: null, ctx: null, src: null, jaw: null, img: null,\n  mouth: null,                 // {cx, lineY, w, chinY} in canvas pixels\n  open: 0, width: 1,           // current (smoothed) mouth shape\n  level: 0,                    // loudness 0..1 (non-ElevenLabs voices)\n  timeline: null, audio: null, // ElevenLabs character timings + the <audio> playing them\n  t0: performance.now(),\n};\n\n/* ---------- mouth shapes ---------- */\nfunction viseme(c) {\n  c = (c || "").toLowerCase();\n  if (c === "a") return [1.0, 1.0];\n  if (c === "e") return [0.75, 1.05];\n  if (c === "i" || c === "y") return [0.6, 1.1];\n  if (c === "o") return [0.85, 0.75];\n  if (c === "u" || c === "w") return [0.6, 0.65];\n  if ("mbp".includes(c)) return [0.0, 0.95];\n  if ("fv".includes(c)) return [0.2, 1.0];\n  if (/[a-z]/.test(c)) return [0.45, 1.0];\n  return [0.0, 1.0];                          // space / punctuation = closed\n}\nfunction targetShape() {\n  const tl = S.timeline, a = S.audio;\n  if (tl && a && !a.paused) {\n    const t = a.currentTime;\n    let lo = 0, hi = tl.starts.length - 1, i = -1;\n    while (lo <= hi) { const mid = (lo + hi) >> 1; if (tl.starts[mid] <= t) { i = mid; lo = mid + 1; } else hi = mid - 1; }\n    if (i >= 0 && t <= (tl.ends[i] || tl.starts[i]) + 0.06) return viseme(tl.chars[i]);\n    return [0, 1];\n  }\n  return [Math.min(1, S.level * 6), 1];\n}\n\n/* ---------- setup ---------- */\nfunction coverRect(iw, ih, cw, ch) {\n  const s = Math.max(cw / iw, ch / ih);\n  return { s, dx: (cw - iw * s) / 2, dy: (ch - ih * s) / 2 };\n}\nfunction loadImage(url) {\n  return new Promise((res, rej) => { const i = new Image(); i.crossOrigin = "anonymous"; i.onload = () => res(i); i.onerror = rej; i.src = url; });\n}\nasync function findMouth(img) {\n  try {\n    const { FaceLandmarker, FilesetResolver } = await import(`${MP}/vision_bundle.mjs`);\n    const vision = await FilesetResolver.forVisionTasks(`${MP}/wasm`);\n    const fl = await FaceLandmarker.createFromOptions(vision, { baseOptions: { modelAssetPath: MODEL }, runningMode: "IMAGE", numFaces: 1 });\n    const lm = fl.detect(img).faceLandmarks[0];\n    fl.close();\n    if (!lm) return null;\n    const P = (k) => ({ x: lm[k].x * img.naturalWidth, y: lm[k].y * img.naturalHeight });\n    const L = P(61), R = P(291), up = P(13), lo = P(14), chin = P(152);\n    return { cx: (L.x + R.x) / 2, lineY: (up.y + lo.y) / 2, w: Math.hypot(R.x - L.x, R.y - L.y), chinY: chin.y };\n  } catch (e) {\n    console.warn("Face detection failed, using config.mouth / default position", e);\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n\nasync function init() {\n  if ((CFG.avatarMode || "photo") !== "photo") return;\n  const box = document.querySelector(".avatar");\n  let img;\n  try { img = await loadImage(CFG.facePhoto || "media/face.jpg"); }\n  catch (e) { console.warn("No media/face.jpg - photo avatar off"); return; }\n\n  // mouth position in photo pixels: auto-detected, or config.mouth (fractions of the photo), or a default guess\n  let m = await findMouth(img);\n  if (!m) {\n    const f = CFG.mouth || { x: 0.5, y: 0.62, w: 0.16, chin: 0.74 };\n    m = { cx: f.x * img.naturalWidth, lineY: f.y * img.naturalHeight, w: f.w * img.naturalWidth, chinY: (f.chin || f.y + 0.12) * img.naturalHeight };\n  }\n\n  const canvas = document.getElementById("faceCanvas");\n  const dpr = Math.min(2, window.devicePixelRatio || 1);\n  const cw = Math.round(box.clientWidth * dpr), ch = Math.round(box.clientHeight * dpr);\n  canvas.width = cw; canvas.height = ch;\n  const r = coverRect(img.naturalWidth, img.naturalHeight, cw, ch);\n\n  const src = document.createElement("canvas"); src.width = cw; src.height = ch;   // photo at canvas size\n  src.getContext("2d").drawImage(img, r.dx, r.dy, img.naturalWidth * r.s, img.naturalHeight * r.s);\n\n  S.mouth = { cx: r.dx + m.cx * r.s, lineY: r.dy + m.lineY * r.s, w: m.w * r.s, chinY: r.dy + m.chinY * r.s };\n  S.canvas = canvas; S.ctx = canvas.getContext("2d"); S.src = src; S.jaw = document.createElement("canvas");\n  S.ready = true;\n  document.body.classList.add("photoavatar");\n  requestAnimationFrame(frame);\n}\n\n/* ---------- drawing ---------- */\nfunction frame(now) {\n  const { ctx, canvas, src, mouth: M } = S;\n  const [tOpen, tWidth] = targetShape();\n  S.open += (tOpen - S.open) * 0.35;\n  S.width += (tWidth - S.width) * 0.3;\n  const strength = CFG.mouthStrength || 1;\n\n  // gentle head movement (more while talking)\n  const t = (now - S.t0) / 1000, talk = S.open > 0.05 ? 1 : 0.4;\n  const pivotY = M.chinY + (M.chinY - M.lineY) * 2;\n  ctx.clearRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);\n  ctx.save();\n  ctx.translate(M.cx, pivotY);\n  ctx.rotate(Math.sin(t * 0.9) * 0.006 * talk);\n  ctx.translate(-M.cx, -pivotY + Math.sin(t * 1.3) * 1.2 * talk);\n  ctx.drawImage(src, 0, 0);\n\n  const h = S.open * M.w * 0.28 * strength;     // how far the mouth opens (pixels)\n  if (h > 0.6) {\n    const mw = M.w * 0.92 * S.width;\n    const L = M.cx - mw / 2, R = M.cx + mw / 2, y = M.lineY;\n    // inside of the mouth: a soft lens shape between the lips\n    ctx.save();\n    ctx.filter = "blur(0.8px)";\n    ctx.fillStyle = "rgb(58,20,22)";\n    ctx.beginPath();\n    ctx.moveTo(L, y);\n    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(M.cx, y - h * 0.15, R, y);\n    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(M.cx, y + h * 1.9, L, y);\n    ctx.fill();\n    if (h > M.w * 0.1) {                         // a hint of upper teeth\n      ctx.fillStyle = "rgba(214,204,194,0.59)";\n      ctx.beginPath();\n      ctx.ellipse(M.cx, y - 1 + (h * 0.28 + 1) / 2, mw * 0.3, (h * 0.28 + 1) / 2, 0, 0, Math.PI * 2);\n      ctx.fill();\n    }\n    ctx.restore();\n    // lower lip + jaw moved down by h, feathered so it blends into the cheeks and chin\n    const jw = M.w * 2.0, rh = (M.chinY - M.lineY) * 1.35;\n    const J = S.jaw; J.width = Math.ceil(jw); J.height = Math.ceil(rh + h + 1);\n    const jc = J.getContext("2d");\n    jc.clearRect(0, 0, J.width, J.height);\n    jc.drawImage(src, M.cx - jw / 2, M.lineY, jw, rh, 0, h, jw, rh);\n    jc.globalCompositeOperation = "destination-in";\n    jc.save();\n    const rx = jw / 2, ry = rh * 0.52;\n    jc.translate(jw / 2, h + rh * 0.5); jc.scale(1, ry / rx);\n    const g = jc.createRadialGradient(0, 0, 0, 0, 0, rx);\n    g.addColorStop(0, "rgba(0,0,0,1)"); g.addColorStop(0.75, "rgba(0,0,0,1)"); g.addColorStop(1, "rgba(0,0,0,0)");\n    jc.fillStyle = g; jc.fillRect(-rx * 2, -rx * 2, rx * 4, rx * 4);\n    jc.restore();\n    jc.globalCompositeOperation = "source-over";\n    ctx.drawImage(J, M.cx - jw / 2, M.lineY);\n  }\n  ctx.restore();\n\n  if (CFG.avatarDebug) {                         // shows where it thinks the mouth and chin are\n    ctx.strokeStyle = "lime"; ctx.lineWidth = 2;\n    ctx.strokeRect(M.cx - M.w / 2, M.lineY - 2, M.w, 4);\n    ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(M.cx - 20, M.chinY); ctx.lineTo(M.cx + 20, M.chinY); ctx.stroke();\n  }\n  requestAnimationFrame(frame);\n}\n\n/* ---------- API for app.js ---------- */\nwindow.TwinAvatar = {\n  get ready() { return S.ready; },\n  get state() { return { open: +S.open.toFixed(2), timeline: !!S.timeline, playing: !!(S.audio && !S.audio.paused) }; },\n  setLevel(v) { S.level = v; },                                  // loudness 0..1\n  speakWith(audioEl, chars, starts, ends) {                     // ElevenLabs timings for this clip\n    S.audio = audioEl; S.timeline = chars && chars.length ? { chars, starts, ends } : null;\n  },\n  stop() { S.timeline = null; S.audio = null; },\n};\ninit();\n',
    'README.md': '# DIGITALTWIN: AI twin of an IHS teacher\n\nDIGITALTWIN is a live, talking AI version of a teacher at The Indian High Group of Schools.\nStudents speak to it (WebRTC live voice) or type. It answers **her subject** (Physics: NCERT Class 11 notes)\nand **general knowledge / study questions**, in her style and **her cloned voice** (ElevenLabs), with her face on screen.\n\n## How it works\n\n```\nStudent (browser) ──WebRTC──► OpenAI Realtime (listens, turn-taking, writes text)\n      │                            │ calls tool "ask_teacher"\n      └─HTTPS──► Backend (FastAPI on Lambda)\n                   /api/ask    Luna: subject chapter / general / unsuitable\n                               Sol:  answer from the chapter notes, or general knowledge\n                   /api/speak  ElevenLabs: text -> her cloned voice (sentence by sentence)\nAvatar: her photo (frontend/media/face.jpg) comes alive in the browser: lips move in sync with her\n        voice using ElevenLabs character timings (avatar.js). Set avatarMode: "video" in config.js for video loops.\n```\n\n- 📘 badge = from the class notes · 🤖 badge = general knowledge.\n- No class code. **Set an OpenAI budget limit and ElevenLabs usage alerts**, and only share the link with students.\n- Without ElevenLabs keys in `.env`, the app uses OpenAI\'s standard voice.\n\n## Folder map\n\n```\nDigitaltwin/\n  backend/            Lambda app (FastAPI + Mangum)\n    main.py           API routes: /api/session, /api/ask, /api/health\n    brain.py          Luna routing + Sol answering + all prompts\n    persona.md        ← EDIT: how the teacher talks\n    chapters.json     chapter list + topics (used for routing)\n    kb/               ch1.md … ch7.md notes (created by extract.py)\n    Dockerfile, requirements.txt, .env.example\n  frontend/           static website (no build step)\n    index.html, app.js, style.css\n    config.js         ← EDIT: API URL + teacher name\n    media/            face.jpg, idleloop.mp4, talkloop.mp4 (from makeloops.ps1)\n  scripts/\n    extract.py        PDFs → clean Markdown notes (equations as LaTeX)\n    makeloops.ps1     her video → avatar loops + voice sample\n    deploy.ps1        Docker → ECR → Lambda + Function URL\n```\n\n---\n\n## Step-by-step\n\n### Step 0: Install once (Windows)\n- Python 3.12, **Docker Desktop** (running), **AWS CLI v2**, ffmpeg (`winget install ffmpeg`)\n- `aws configure` → your access key, secret, region `me-central-1`\n- OpenAI dashboard → **Billing → set a monthly budget limit** (e.g. $20)\n\nUnzip the project, open PowerShell in the `Digitaltwin` folder:\n```powershell\npython -m venv venv\nvenv\\Scripts\\activate\npip install -r scripts\\requirements.txt -r backend\\requirements.txt\ncopy backend\\.env.example backend\\.env\nnotepad backend\\.env          # OpenAI key, TEACHER_NAME, SUBJECT, ElevenLabs key + voice ID\n```\nCheck the exact model names your key can use, and fix them in `.env` if they differ:\n```powershell\npython -c "from dotenv import load_dotenv; load_dotenv(\'backend/.env\'); from openai import OpenAI; print(sorted(m.id for m in OpenAI().models.list()))"\n```\n\n### Step 1: Check the PDFs (free, no API calls)\n```powershell\npython scripts\\extract.py --src "C:\\Users\\OMC-LP185\\Downloads\\PHYSICS" --check\n```\nIt lists every chapter with its page count and warns about wrong or duplicate files.\n⚠️ In your folder, **CH-6 is exactly the same size as CH-1 (1,106 KB)**, but Chapter 6 should be the biggest one (35 pages).\nIt is probably a duplicate download. If the check flags it, download Chapter 6 again from the NCERT site.\n\n### Step 2: Turn the PDFs into notes (about 15 min, about $2 one-time)\n```powershell\npython scripts\\extract.py --src "C:\\Users\\OMC-LP185\\Downloads\\PHYSICS"\n```\nThis creates `backend\\kb\\ch1.md … ch7.md`. If it stops, run it again; it resumes from where it stopped.\n**Open 2-3 files and spot-check them**: equations readable? Examples complete?\nYou can also add the teacher\'s own tips or notes at the end of any chapter file.\n\n### Step 3: Fill in her persona\nEdit `backend\\persona.md` using her video and lesson recordings: greeting, favourite phrases,\nhow she explains, how she corrects mistakes. **This is what makes it sound like her.**\n\n### Step 4: Avatar from her 1-minute video\nWatch the video and note a stretch where she is **talking** and a stretch where she is **quiet or nodding**:\n```powershell\n.\\scripts\\makeloops.ps1 -Video "C:\\path\\teacher.mp4" -TalkStart 00:00:12 -TalkSeconds 8 -IdleStart 00:00:45 -IdleSeconds 6\n```\nThis creates `frontend\\media\\face.jpg`, `talkloop.mp4` and `idleloop.mp4`, plus `voicesample.wav` (kept for Version 2).\n\n### Step 5: Test locally\nTerminal 1 (backend):\n```powershell\ncd backend\nuvicorn main:app --port 8000\n```\nOpen http://localhost:8000/api/health. All 7 chapters should show `true`.\n\nTerminal 2 (frontend):\n```powershell\ncd frontend\npython -m http.server 5500\n```\nOpen **http://localhost:5500**, then:\n1. Type: *"What is the difference between distance and displacement?"* → expect a 📘 Ch 2 answer.\n2. Click **Start live class**, allow the microphone, and ask by voice: *"Explain Newton\'s second law."*\n3. Ask a follow-up: *"Give me one example."*\n4. Ask general knowledge: *"Which is the largest planet?"* → expect a 🤖 answer in her voice.\n\n### Step 6: Deploy the backend to AWS (Docker → ECR → Lambda)\n```powershell\n.\\scripts\\deploy.ps1 -Tag v1\n```\nThe first run creates the ECR repo, IAM role, Lambda (1 GB RAM, 60 s timeout) and a public Function URL.\nIt prints the **API URL**. Open `API URL/api/health` to confirm it works.\nEach later update: `.\\scripts\\deploy.ps1 -Tag v2` (always use a new tag).\n\n### Step 7: Host the frontend (HTTPS is required for the microphone)\n1. Put the API URL into `frontend\\config.js` (`apiBase`, no trailing slash) and set `teacherName`.\n2. Zip the **contents** of the `frontend` folder.\n3. AWS Console → **Amplify** → *Create new app* → **Deploy without Git** → upload the zip.\n   You get an `https://….amplifyapp.com` link.\n4. Put that link in `backend\\.env` → `ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://….amplifyapp.com`, then run `.\\scripts\\deploy.ps1 -Tag v2`.\n\n### Step 8: Pilot\n- Run 30 test questions: 20 from the chapters, 5 outside the syllabus, 5 follow-ups.\n- Have the teacher review 20 answers for **tone** and fix `persona.md` (then redeploy).\n- To see which questions the notes didn\'t cover: CloudWatch → Log groups → `/aws/lambda/digitaltwin-brain` →\n  search `"from_notes": false`. Add those topics to the notes.\n\n---\n\n## Costs (approximate)\n| Part | Cost |\n|---|---|\n| Notes extraction (one-time) | about $2 |\n| Typed question (Luna + Sol, chapter context) | about $0.01-0.04 |\n| Live voice (OpenAI Realtime) | the main cost: billed per minute of audio, so watch usage |\n| Lambda, ECR, Amplify | free tier / a few cents |\n\n## Troubleshooting\n| Problem | Fix |\n|---|---|\n| `Voice error` | Check `ELEVENLABS_API_KEY` / `ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID` in `.env`, then restart the backend |\n| `Model error: … model not found` | Fix the model IDs in `.env` (see Step 0), then redeploy |\n| `OpenAI realtime error` on Start | Check `REALTIME_MODEL`, `REALTIME_VOICE`, `TRANSCRIBE_MODEL` in `.env`; check the Realtime API is enabled for your key |\n| CORS error in the browser console | `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` must contain the exact site URL. Do **not** enable CORS on the Function URL itself |\n| Function URL gives 403 | Lambda console → your function → Configuration → Function URL → check auth type NONE and the resource-based policy |\n| Microphone blocked | The site must be on `https://` or `localhost` |\n| Answers are slow | Set `REASONING_EFFORT=low` (default). Chapter 6 is the largest, so it is slightly slower |\n| Avatar doesn\'t switch | Check the media files exist; the photo fallback pulses instead |\n\n## Version 2 ideas\n- **Live lip-sync**: a streaming avatar service that accepts our ElevenLabs audio\n- **Intro clip**: ElevenLabs Avatar video of her, played when the app opens\n- Physics Part II chapters: add PDFs → run extract.py → add them to chapters.json\n- Step-by-step drawing videos for numericals, quiz mode, teacher admin page\n',
}

